{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":170946,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8f13d3dd-1101-4b08-9de6-4bf033ea9a2e","total_cost_usd":0.755366,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36592,"cache_read_input_tokens":20616,"output_tokens":14195,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36592,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":14195,"cache_read_input_tokens":20616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36592},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":24158,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.024253,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":14195,"cacheReadInputTokens":20616,"cacheCreationInputTokens":36592,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.731113,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\":     { \"slots_crushed\": 1, \"slots_uncrushed\": 2, \"hand_tetherable\": true },\n    \"medium\":    { \"slots_crushed\": 2, \"slots_uncrushed\": 4, \"hand_tetherable\": true },\n    \"oversized\": { \"slots_crushed\": 6, \"slots_uncrushed\": 12, \"hand_tetherable\": false }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_hull_panel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Hull Panel\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 140.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 20,\n      \"notes\": \"Curved skin plate off something that already burned once — the commonest thing in the low sky and the piece every player learns to latch on first.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 380.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 14,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded aluminium lattice that crushes down well; two slots of honest tonnage and the first piece that makes the jetpack feel heavy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_booster_ring\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Booster Ring\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 460.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"Interstage collar from a launcher that never made orbit — the heaviest hand-tetherable piece in the band, and a deliberate test of whether the player tows gently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"insulation_blanket_wad\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Insulation Blanket Wad\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 60.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 18,\n      \"notes\": \"A balled-up wad of multi-layer foil: almost free to tow, but it still costs a full crushed slot, so it is the piece that teaches slot cost and mass are different currencies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fairing_shard\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Fairing Shard\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 110.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"A composite wedge off a shattered payload fairing — light, plentiful, and the reliable filler that keeps a lazy run breaking even.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_camera_dome\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Camera Dome\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 95.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"Star-cracked optical dome that still glints on a slow cycle; the player's first fragile piece, cheap enough to lose and instructive enough to matter.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"battered_antenna_whip\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Battered Antenna Whip\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 70.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A bent whip antenna on its feed block — the lightest fragile piece in the game, so a suborbital player can practise a gentle landing without much at stake.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"derelict_upper_stage\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Derelict Upper Stage\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1150.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"A whole dead kick stage tumbling slowly; crane-cable only and therefore out of reach in the shipping slice, present so the oversized class exists in the lowest band the player ever flies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"satellite_bus_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Satellite Bus Frame\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 700.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 14,\n      \"notes\": \"The structural box a satellite was built around, stripped of everything soft — the low band's bread-and-butter haul and the first piece that visibly slows the ride home.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 520.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded array wing with half its cells starred; never crushable, so it pays four uncrushed slots forever, and it is the archetypal fragile decision of the shipping slice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 300.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"A dense steel flywheel can — one slot of concentrated mass, which is what makes the low band heavier per slot than suborbital without filling the hold faster.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"propellant_tank_shell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Propellant Tank Shell\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 620.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A punctured titanium sphere that crushes flat with a satisfying report; bulky before the compactor touches it, ordinary after.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gyro_package\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gyro Package\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 260.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"A sealed inertial unit, solid and unglamorous — the piece a cautious player fills the last slot with when the shield plate is already low.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"parabolic_dish_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Parabolic Dish Section\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 480.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A quarter-segment of a comms dish, thin-skinned and awkward on the line; it spawns off the clumps and high in the band, so reaching it is a real burn.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"star_tracker_head\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Star Tracker Head\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 210.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A shaded optical head the size of a coffee can — the rarest thing in the low band and the cheapest fragile piece to tow, which makes the detour tempting rather than obvious.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tumbling_comsat_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tumbling Comsat Core\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2000.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"An intact comsat body spinning end over end; crane-cable only, deferred with the crane magnet, and the rehearsal object for the capstone capture.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dense_avionics_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dense Avionics Core\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1000.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A potted flight-computer block, solid metal and boards all the way through — the high band's workhorse and, at half a tonne per slot, the reason a full hold up here needs extra passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_solar_wing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Solar Wing\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 820.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A long array wing snapped mid-span, still glinting; the most frequently met fragile piece in the game and the one most often lost to a hot entry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"iridium_battery_stack\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Iridium Battery Stack\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1150.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A strapped column of cells wrapped in shielding — the heaviest hand-tetherable piece authored, and the clearest single expression of 'the valuable stuff fights you'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"platinum_thruster_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Platinum Thruster Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 540.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"Four scorched attitude nozzles on a common manifold, crammed with precious metal; one crushed slot, and the densest thing per slot a hand magnet can hold.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"optical_telescope_barrel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Optical Telescope Barrel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 900.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A baffled tube with the primary mirror still seated — heavy, fragile, uncrushable, and the piece that makes a player choose between a soft landing and one more pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cryo_instrument_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cryo Instrument Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 430.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A frosted dewar off a science payload, thin-walled and unforgiving; small enough to slip into a nearly full hold, fragile enough to be the first thing a hard touchdown wrecks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gold_foil_bus_module\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gold Foil Bus Module\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 980.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A foil-wrapped equipment bay torn cleanly off its bus — crushable, solid, and the safe high-band haul when the shield plate will not stand another hot pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mirrored_survey_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Mirrored Survey Array\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2900.0,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"A segmented mirror panel the size of a barn door: fragile and oversized at once, crane-cable only, deferred with the high band — it exists to preview the exact class Mr. Armstrong's satellite belongs to.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"piece_count\": 8,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.103,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 308.125\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"piece_count\": 8,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.179,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 636.25\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"piece_count\": 8,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 1090.0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"Mass rises about 3.5x from suborbital to high on the plain per-piece mean (308.1 -> 636.3 -> 1090.0 kg), and about 4.4x if the crane-only oversized pieces are excluded (187.9 -> 441.4 -> 831.4 kg). That is the GDD 2.3.7 bet stated in numbers: the better the haul, the worse the ride home.\",\n    \"The figure that actually reaches the physics is mass per crushed slot, because slots are what cap a hold. Suborbital runs ~95 kg/slot for smalls and ~210 for mediums; low runs ~257 and ~290; high runs ~485 for both. A 6-slot starting hold therefore weighs roughly 0.6-1.3 t from suborbital, ~1.7 t from low, and ~2.9 t from high. Against the Researcher's 1400 kg staged ship that is beta 267 empty rising to roughly 480-780 loaded from the lower bands and ~820 from the high band, i.e. two to three times the passes an empty ship needs. The catalog carries the band-to-band difficulty differential the Researcher warned entry speed alone could not (his note: only 1.35x flux from suborbital to high), which is exactly the beta lever he pointed at.\",\n    \"Ship mass is not mine to set, and this is the one place the catalog constrains it. GDD 2.3.5 says a full hold at starting storage roughly doubles the rocket's mass; that holds here if the staged ship is around 1 t and the player is filling suborbital slots with mediums. If the crew prices the ship far below that, every mass in this catalog should be scaled by the same factor rather than re-authored piecewise.\",\n    \"The fragile gradient is spawn-weighted, not counted: suborbital 9/87 = 0.103, low 12/67 = 0.179, high 14/56 = 0.250. By piece count the three bands would read 2/8, 3/8 and 4/8 (0.25/0.375/0.50), which is why the fragile pieces carry the lowest weights in every band — a fragile piece has to be rare in encounter terms, not just rare in the type list.\",\n    \"No piece is strictly best, because mass and slot cost are deliberately decoupled. The insulation blanket wad is nearly free to tow and still costs a whole crushed slot; the platinum thruster cluster is one slot holding 540 kg. So the greedy choice at the tether is not the greedy choice at the hold, and the player has to decide which resource is scarce on this particular run.\",\n    \"Every size class and the fragile flag are all reachable inside the shipping slice. Suborbital and low each hold five and three small pieces, two and four mediums, and two and three fragiles respectively, so nothing about the vocabulary waits on the deferred high band.\",\n    \"Oversized is one piece per band and nothing more: derelict upper stage, tumbling comsat core, mirrored survey array. All three are crane-cable only and expected to be unreachable this semester. The high band's is fragile on purpose, so the fragile-and-oversized class the win condition belongs to exists in the catalog before the satellite does.\",\n    \"Mr. Armstrong's satellite is deliberately not in this catalog. The Researcher puts it above the high band at ~360 km, and the charter asks for exactly three bands; it is a named capstone object, not a spawn-table entry, and pricing it as ordinary loot would be wrong.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":111422,"ttft_stream_ms":1544,"time_to_request_ms":233,"type":"result","duration_ms":169393,"uuid":"11d06ef8-f051-452a-af9d-ca476bc0172a"}
